# Force HTTPS and www redirect
http://atteste.art/* https://atteste.art/:splat 301!
http://www.atteste.art/* https://atteste.art/:splat 301!
https://www.atteste.art/* https://atteste.art/:splat 301!

# Block direct access to internal strategy docs and operational scripts
# (robots.txt is advisory; this is the real gate)
/marketing/* /404.html 404!
/scripts/*   /404.html 404!
/.claude/*   /404.html 404!
/docs/*      /404.html 404!
/CLAUDE.md   /404.html 404!
/README.md   /404.html 404!

# NFC tag verify URLs — taps on /v/{certId} are intercepted by the
# Atteste app via Universal Links / App Links (see /.well-known/
# apple-app-site-association and /assetlinks.json). When the app
# is NOT installed, the OS opens the URL in a browser; we redirect
# to the existing Firebase Hosting verify page so the cert still
# resolves. App-installed users never see this redirect — the OS
# routes the URL into the app before the network request fires.
/v/* https://atteste-b6409.web.app/verify/:splat 302

# Referral invite links — /r/{code} rewrites (200, path preserved) to the
# landing page, which reads the code from the path via JS and offers store
# badges + a "continue on the web" hand-off to the Flutter web app's
# /r/:code route (auto-redeem after sign-up). Like /v/*, installed apps
# intercept /r/* via Universal Links (AASA component added alongside this
# rule) before the request ever reaches Netlify.
/r/* /r/index.html 200

# One-click unsubscribe (RFC 8058) for outreach + lifecycle mail. Mirrors the
# /v/* pattern above: atteste.art is served by Netlify, so a Firebase Hosting
# rewrite alone is unreachable here — this hop is what makes the branded URL
# resolve to the `emailUnsubscribe` Cloud Function.
#
# THE WHOLE PAYLOAD IS THE QUERY STRING (?u=<address>&t=<hmac>). Netlify appends
# the incoming query to a destination that carries none of its own, which is why
# this rule has no :splat and no query params on the target — do not add either.
# If this line is ever rewritten, re-verify a real link end-to-end: a redirect
# that drops ?u/?t yields "400 — This unsubscribe link is not valid", which is
# strictly worse than having no unsubscribe link at all, because mailbox
# providers action one-click on the recipient's behalf and record the failure.
#
# 302, not 301: a permanent redirect gets cached by intermediaries, and this
# target may need to move.
/unsubscribe https://atteste-b6409.web.app/unsubscribe 302

# Site bot (Phase 1) — same-origin rewrite, NOT a redirect.
#
# 200 = Netlify proxies internally, so the browser only ever sees
# https://atteste.art/api/chat. That is what keeps the widget inside the
# existing `connect-src 'self'` CSP with no header change: a 30x to
# /.netlify/functions/chat would expose a second origin and break it.
# The function itself enforces origin allowlist, rate limit, and kill switch.
/api/chat  /.netlify/functions/chat  200

